{"id":"0161-a-feedback-shifters-mode-byte-picks-the-same-five-lengths","path":"inferences/roland-sc8850-01/0161-a-feedback-shifters-mode-byte-picks-the-same-five-lengths.json","unitId":"roland-sc8850-01","state":"standing","level":"investigating","why":"no model has been rendered and compared with the unit","verdict":null,"standing":"unmodelled","rounds":2,"madeAt":"2026-09-21T16:26:06+00:00","madeBy":"backup/what-a-feedback-pitch-shifters-mode-byte-is-the-length-of.py, backup/publish-the-feedback-shifters-loop.py, backup/write-the-feedback-shifter-inference.py, backup/add-the-repeated-arms-round-to-the-feedback-shifter-inference.py","about":{"scope":"unit","class":null,"types":["01 61"],"addresses":["40 03 05","40 03 07"],"checkedOnUnits":[]},"title":{"names":[{"name":"Fb P.Shifter","page":218,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"}],"more":0,"parameters":[{"name":"Feedback","page":218},{"name":"Mode","page":218}],"parametersMore":0,"document":"roland-sc-8850-owners-manual-en"},"printedTypes":[{"type":"01 61","name":"Fb P.Shifter"}],"supersededBy":null,"retractedBecause":null,"claim":"Type `01 61`'s mode byte picks a length, and the five it picks stand in the ratio 3 : 4 : 6 : 8 : 12 -- the ratio the single pitch shifter's five windows were measured to stand in. Read as the distance the output holds a copy of itself at, with the shifter two semitones up where four takes of one state land 0.021 ms apart, the five states give 28.505, 38.000, 57.000, 75.995 and 114.026 ms -- against the first state 1.000, 1.333, 2.000, 2.666 and 4.000 where the ratio predicts 1, 1.333, 2, 2.667 and 4, every one of them inside that 0.021. At unison the same five land up to 10.52 ms apart from themselves, five hundred times further, so the reading the ratio rests on is the shifted one and the unison takes bound nothing. Each distance is 0.8906 of the window at the same state, to four figures across all five, and that multiple is not explained here.","named":null,"whyNotNamed":null,"adds":"This type carried no structural reading. It prints one shifter where the type beside it prints two and it prints a feedback byte that one does not, and the only claims naming it were the two that run across every type. What the window claim found was read off an artefact rate on one type; this is a distance in milliseconds on another, taken with a different stage, and it was predicted before the takes were made rather than read out of them.","refutedBy":"A state of the mode byte whose distance is not the ratio the five lengths stand in, by more than four takes of that state land apart. Every state is now bounded at 0.021 ms, which is the reading's own grid step, so any of the five can refute this and the fifth is no longer the one that cannot.","couldHaveBeenRefutedBy":null,"whatItWouldChange":["Rendering this type needs the same table of five lengths the type beside it needs, and not a second one read off its own page. The two print the same `1 - 5` against a byte with no unit beside it and the two answer to the same five ratios.","A byte printed as a bare count of states on this family has now been read as a length twice, on two types, by two quantities and two stages. The measurement that settles such a byte is a sweep of something else while the counted byte is held, and it is cheap."],"grounds":{"measurements":[{"file":"data/units/roland-sc8850-01/efx-time/01-61-07-where-the-loop-puts-its-copy-at-each-mode.json","within":"efx-time/01-61-07-where-the-loop-puts-its-copy-at-each-mode.json","keys":["readings[value=0].ms","readings[value=1].ms","readings[value=3].ms","readings[value=4].ms","floor_ms","settings_taken_twice","settings_asked","held"],"values":[27.875,39.4583,78.5625,125.9583,7.9166,[2],[0,1,2,3,4],[{"address":"40 42 22","bytes":"01"},{"address":"40 12 31","bytes":"00"},{"address":"40 03 03","bytes":"40"},{"address":"40 03 04","bytes":"40"},{"address":"40 03 05","bytes":"54"},{"address":"40 03 06","bytes":"00"},{"address":"40 03 08","bytes":"40